    "result_text": "Done. The suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**1. `Owner.assignCustomerCode(int)`** \u2014 now builds the `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` code, reading the `city` field for the prefix. The parameter is now interpreted as the per-city count. CC stays at 1.\n\n**2. `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 one-line change to pass the per-city count (owners already in the same city, case-insensitive) instead of the total owner count.\n\n## Derived values\n\n`membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) in `OwnerMapper` reads `getCustomerCode()` directly, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 no change needed there.\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n\nI kept the loop/filtering in the service (which already held the owner collection) as a single stream expression, so neither changed function grew in complexity: both stayed at low CC, and I touched only the two files that genuinely had to change. I avoided moving the per-city counting logic into the large `Owner` class (which would have raised that method's complexity while paying the class's full `WMC_other`).",
